/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  flowsheetDict --- ED10 a component the stack does not model, DECLARED to
                    pass through it
  ===========================================================================

  ed01's stack and ed01's NaCl diluate, with ONE change: the diluate feed
  also carries a little benzene (0.01 kmol/h against 17.9 kmol/h of water,
  about 0.78 kg/h -- above benzene's solubility in water, so in the plant it
  would ride as droplets of a second liquid phase).

      diluateFeed (+ benzene) -> +-----------------+ -> diluate (+ benzene)
                                 |   ED stack      |
      concentrateFeed       ->   | (CMX/AMX, N=100)| -> concentrate
                                 +-----------------+

  WHAT THIS SHOWS.  The stack models the aqueous solvent and the IONS:
  every other component must cross its declared bridge to one catalogued
  ion (`choupoSolve --describe-units` prints that contract).  Benzene is
  not an ion, so without the `passThrough` block below the run is REFUSED
  before any unit runs, naming benzene and both remedies.  With the block,
  benzene is ACCEPTED as a DECLARED APPROXIMATION: it enters none of the
  stack's equations, every mole of it leaves in the outlet the case names
  (`fate diluate`), and it is in every balance (mass, elements, energy).

  THE PASS-THROUGH IS A DECLARED APPROXIMATION, NOT A RESULT.  The run
  records it on the problem-divergence channel -- printed ABOVE the KPIs,
  in the result JSON and in converged/problemDivergence -- with the reason
  below.  What it sets aside is real: an organic film on the membranes,
  a change in the channel's conductivity, any benzene the membranes would
  sorb.  The stack computes none of them, and says so.

  Benzene moves no stack number: the molalities are taken on the water and
  benzene is not an ion of the channel, so the same case run WITHOUT benzene
  gives every KPI (voltage, demin ratio, limiting current, specific energy)
  to the last printed digit -- check_unit_acceptance runs that twin.  (Read
  against ed01 the voltage differs in the fourth figure: this case was
  sealed against the Choupo-2608 catalogue, whose Na and Cl records carry
  different curated diffusivities from the 2607 records ed01 was sealed
  with.  That is the catalogue, not the benzene.)

  The thermophysical package is ed01's ideal liquid with benzene added (see
  constant/thermoPhysPropDict): it prices the streams for the balances and
  does not represent the second liquid phase either.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

// stream state lives on disk in 0/ (per-stream files); flowsheetDict is TOPOLOGY only

units
(
    {
        name        edStack;
        type        electrodialysisStack;
        inputs      ( diluateFeed  concentrateFeed );
        outputs     ( diluate  concentrate );

        operation
        {
            N_cellpairs       100;
            current           8.0;        // A (raw SI) -- applied current (below i_lim, see log)
            xi                0.9;         // current efficiency (announced default)
            membraneArea      0.2 m2;     // per membrane
            channelThickness  0.5 mm;     // spacer gap
            channelLength     0.4 m;      // flow path (for the Leveque k)
            linearVelocity    0.05 m/s;   // cross-flow velocity
            E_electrodes      1.5;        // V (raw SI) -- lumped electrode overpotential (announced)
            membrane          CMX_AMX;    // IEM pair (data/standards or constant/membranes)
        }

        //  A DECLARED APPROXIMATION (DEV.md 4c C188): benzene crosses the
        //  stack outside its equations.  The fates the stack offers are
        //  `diluate` and `concentrate` (the outlet that carries ALL of it);
        //  no split fraction is offered, and the reason is required.
        passThrough
        {
            benzene { fate diluate; }
            reason  "trace organic in a second liquid phase riding with the diluate; the stack's ion transport does not act on it";
        }

        // The DC power drawn by the stack is published on an energy wire as
        // W_electric (P = U*I), mirroring the turbine/compressor shaft-wire
        // convention; the rectifier (electricLoad) absorbs it.
        energyOutputs
        (
            { name power;  kind work;  expression "W_electric";  unit W; }
        );
    }
    {
        name        rectifier;
        type        electricLoad;
        operation   { eta 1.0; }
        energyInputs
        (
            { from edStack.power;  kind work;  target W_shaft; }
        );
    }
);
